  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1111 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nNot much to discuss as hot and dry weather will continue for several\ndays. There is an outside chance of storms along the Colorado border\nTuesday evening, however, a more likely scenario is that all the\nconvection will remain west of the FA. Otherwise, the long and short\nof the synoptic pattern is that a large and strong mid level anticyclone\nwill continue to prevail across the greater region through the entire\nweek. This will keep the hot and dry weather pattern continue across\nsouthwest Kansas. Temperatures will not change much in this stagnant\nweather pattern. Highs will peak each day in the upper 90s to lower\n100s. Lows will be from the upper 60s to upper 70s. South-central\nKansas will see afternoon heat indices in the low 100s. Will have\nto watch each day if it could make to advisory criteria. Right now,\nit looks less likely, perhaps with the exception on Thursday. Lastly,\nno major fire weather days are expected as both afternoon relative\nhumidity and afternoon winds will be on the marginal side.",
